{"kind":"request","text":"Please review draft 5 of notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md at 4c082db8b9dde79dcd2c6f97aca7426d92c93052 on planner/sales-applications-20261019 (request 7f569087, promise 28988cd9; replaces 53a9f9de). One Markdown path on main 2127d5c5. It answers 19d0bbfd. F1: supply is four acts with fixed grants (supply-technical, supply-product, supply-legal, supply-security), each guarded by the requirement's domain and by the signer being the assigned expert party; review-answer, send-back, ask-expert and decline-requirement are under one grant bid.review held by the owner and the sales engineer, with a reviewer-party signer guard when set; approvals are per kind under bid.price and bid.legal; the agent holds only bid.draft (draft-answer, flag) and bid.intake, and asking an expert is a person's act; the text says routing offers an act and only the grant and guards admit it (5.1, 5.3). F2: intake creates the price and terms approvals in requested, bound to their requirements; a later supply resets the approval; assemble is guarded on every row of every confirmed import reviewed or declined with a reason, no proposed mapping, both approvals granted at the current revisions they cover, and a rendering at those revisions; it writes an assembly item naming the rendering digest, answer revisions and approval entries; submit names that exact assembly; C3 now refuses assembly while a row is unresolved and while the terms approval is stale, then resolves all forty rows (5.2, 5.3, 8). F3: publication is pending from the send and confirmed only when the destination's receipt (sending scope and incarnation, source fact, send ordinal, path, content digest) is read back with a matching digest, by a record-publication act; unknown holds and is not resent; refusals recorded; a later submission or a changed post never inherits a receipt; the published log shows confirmed publications with pending and unknown apart (5.2, 5.3, 6.2, 6.3). F4: retiring a post replaces its file with a notice and rewrites the index, each a publication with its own outcome; deleting the file is deferred (6.2, 6.3, 8). F5: an import holds at most one hundred rows, the complete-read bound of the routed carousel; a larger request is refused at import before any requirement opens; larger matrices deferred; the few-hundred claim is gone (5.2, 5.4, 8). Also: several scopes credited to M2a's interface and M2b's ownership work (5.4). Draft 4 added section 2, Why not just an agent, a product-neutral statement of what the room adds to a personal agent, and a sentence in each application's opening; sections renumbered 2 to 9. Documentation only; no gate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe6e7ef19a22e730c8ea4431277ebe16c32471ae","branch":"planner/sales-applications-20261019","conditions":"exact-head design review of 4c082db8 with architecture, security and simplification conclusions; 19d0bbfd F1 to F5 answered; the definitions fit the landed forms; claims about what exists today are accurate; links resolve; plain English, no product names","head":"4c082db8b9dde79dcd2c6f97aca7426d92c93052","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}